# Every environment variable this repo's code reads, grouped by WHERE it
# belongs — not alphabetically, because the wrong file is exactly the mistake
# this grouping exists to prevent. Placeholder values only; this file is
# committed and public. See docs/onboarding-a-shelter.md and
# docs/h1-decisions.md for the fuller reasoning behind the R2 split below.
#
# ⚠ This file is a reference, not something to copy wholesale into one
# working .env. Section 1's variables are set in the Vercel dashboard, never
# in a local file — see the warning inside that section. Section 2's
# variables belong on an operator's own machine, passed inline per command,
# never saved to a file at all — see that section's warning. Only section 3
# (local development) is meant to actually be copied into a real local env
# file, and even there, read the DATABASE_URL warning before you do.

# ============================================================
# 1. Deployed web app (apps/web) — set in Vercel, Production and
#    Preview environments. NEVER put a real value for anything in this
#    section into a file in this repo, local or otherwise — Vercel's
#    dashboard is the only place these values should exist outside your own
#    memory. Nothing here is read locally unless you export it inline for a
#    one-off command (see section 3 for the local-dev equivalents).
# ============================================================

# Required. The R2 bucket's PUBLIC read URL (a custom domain in front of the
# bucket, e.g. Cloudflare's own CDN domain for it) — this is what
# apps/web/src/image-loader.ts builds real animal photo URLs against.
# Required both at Vercel boot (apps/web/src/api/env.ts's validateEnv) AND
# at build time (apps/web/next.config.ts throws if this is unset on a Vercel
# build) — it's baked into the client bundle, not read live at request time.
# See docs/h1-decisions.md for why both checks exist and aren't redundant.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://cdn.example.com

# Required. Postgres connection string (pooled, for serverless — see
# docs/build-plan.md's Neon setup notes for the pooled-vs-direct
# distinction). Throws at boot in production if unset
# (apps/web/src/instrumentation.ts) and at first use everywhere else
# (apps/web/src/api/env.ts's requireEnv).
#
# ⚠ NEVER put the production connection string in this or any .env file,
# anywhere in this repo, even .gitignore'd ones. packages/db/src/seed.ts
# truncates every table before reseeding, and its --force flag exists
# specifically to permit a non-localhost target — a stray `pnpm db:seed`
# run against a file that happens to still have the production URL in it is
# unrecoverable once real shelter data exists. Pass the production URL
# inline, per command, every time:
#   DATABASE_URL=<neon-url> pnpm --filter @opika/db run db:migrate --prod
# The friction is the safety feature, not an oversight. Since 2026-10-07
# db:migrate, db:seed and onboard:shelter also refuse production without an
# explicit --prod (packages/db/src/prod-guard.ts). Production is identified by
# its Neon compute endpoint id only, never a URL (no password in any file):
# PROD_NEON_ENDPOINT=ep-xxxx  (in the root .env.local, which the scripts read
# for that one key, or in the environment). With it unset, every non-local
# target is refused (fail closed).
# DATABASE_URL=<set in Vercel dashboard — never in a file>

# Required. Signs feed and reveal pagination cursors (HMAC-SHA256) so a
# client can't forge one to skip ahead, reuse a cursor across a changed
# filter set, or reuse a feed cursor as a reveal cursor. Generate a real
# value with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Throws at boot in production if unset, and at first use (any feed.list or
# reveals.list call) everywhere else — see apps/web/src/api/env.ts.
#
# Same rule as DATABASE_URL above: the production value lives in Vercel's
# dashboard only. If you need it locally (rare — most local work should use
# a freshly generated local value, see section 3), pass it inline, never
# save it to a file.
# CURSOR_HMAC_SECRET=<set in Vercel dashboard — never in a file>

# Required. Opens apps/web/src/proxy.ts's pre-launch gate — while
# SITE_IS_PUBLICLY_DISCOVERABLE is false (apps/web/src/seo-flags.ts), every
# request 403s unless it carries this secret (a `?gate=` query parameter or
# the cookie that param mints). Unlike the other secrets in this section,
# this one is read on every single request, not just DB-backed ones — set
# it in Vercel BEFORE deploying any build that requires it (Production AND
# Preview), or the first request to the new deploy 500s. Generate with:
# openssl rand -hex 32. Comes back out of this schema (and this file) in the
# same change that removes the gate — see docs/build-plan.md's launch-gate
# section.
# PRELAUNCH_GATE_SECRET=<set in Vercel dashboard — never in a file>

# Required on the production deployment (KH-Q9). Vercel sends it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` to the daily auth clean-up
# (apps/web/vercel.json `crons` → /api/cron/auth-cleanup), which deletes
# Better Auth rows that are already dead and refuses every call without it.
# A production build fails, and a production instance refuses to boot,
# without a value of at least 32 characters (apps/web/src/api/build-env.ts,
# apps/web/src/api/env.ts), so set it in Vercel's Production environment
# BEFORE deploying the change that adds it. Preview doesn't need it (Vercel
# runs crons on production only). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32.
# Locally, only to call the route by hand: a fresh local value, never the
# production one.
# CRON_SECRET=<set in Vercel dashboard — never in a file>

# Required on EVERY Vercel deployment, Preview included (EM-Q11; widened to
# Preview 2026-10-15, EM-B6). Every rate limiter keys a client IP as `ip:` +
# HMAC-SHA256(RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET, ip) (apps/web/src/api/rate-limit-key.ts),
# so the limiter store (Upstash Redis) never holds an address. Its own secret,
# never LOCATION_HMAC_SECRET or CURSOR_HMAC_SECRET; rotating it only resets the
# rate-limit buckets. A Vercel build (Production or Preview) fails, and such an
# instance refuses to boot, without a value of at least 32 characters
# (apps/web/src/api/build-env.ts, apps/web/src/api/env.ts). Set it in Vercel's
# Production AND Preview environments, a SEPARATE value on each. Off Vercel
# (local dev, CI, the harness) it is optional: unset, each process uses a
# random key of its own (never a value from this repo). VERCEL_ENV=development
# (a pulled Vercel env) counts as local. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32.
# RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET=<set in Vercel dashboard — never in a file>

# ============================================================
# 2. Onboarding script (packages/db/src/onboard-shelter.ts) only — an
#    operator's own machine, never Vercel. The deployed app must never hold
#    R2 WRITE credentials: a compromised deployment (a dependency CVE, a
#    leaked Vercel token, anything) must not be able to overwrite or delete
#    a real shelter's photos. The deployed app only ever needs the R2
#    bucket's PUBLIC read URL (section 1, above) — never these.
#
#    Pass all four inline, per command, exactly like DATABASE_URL and
#    LOCATION_HMAC_SECRET below — don't save real values to a file, even a
#    gitignored one, on principle: a file on disk is one accidental `git
#    add -A` away from becoming a real leak, and there is no legitimate
#    reason this script needs to be run twice in a row without re-supplying
#    its own credentials. See docs/onboarding-a-shelter.md for the full
#    run sequence (dry run first, always).
# ============================================================

# Required for onboard-shelter.ts — BOTH dry-run and --commit, checked
# before anything else runs. Generate one once with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Keep it somewhere you can find it again — the same value must be used
# every time you onboard a shelter, or a shelter onboarded with a different
# secret gets a public location fuzzed against a key nothing else remembers.
# Also in Vercel's Production environment, THE SAME VALUE, since the commit
# that turns production sign-in on (RG-Q10): the registry fuzzes locations
# with it, and a production instance refuses to boot without 32+ characters
# (apps/web/src/api/build-env.ts, locationSecretProblem). Not in Preview.
# LOCATION_HMAC_SECRET=<generate with: openssl rand -hex 32>

# Required for onboard-shelter.ts — both dry-run and --commit (the script
# reads real files and writes to Postgres in both modes; only the R2 upload
# below is --commit-only). Use Neon's DIRECT connection string here, not the
# pooled one from section 1 — docs/onboarding-a-shelter.md explains why.
# DATABASE_URL=<neon direct connection string>

# Required for --commit only (a dry run validates local photo files but
# never uploads). All four values come from Cloudflare's dashboard: R2 →
# your bucket → Manage API tokens.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=
# Note: there is no separate R2_ENDPOINT variable — the upload endpoint is
# derived from R2_ACCOUNT_ID alone (packages/db/src/image-pipeline/
# variants.ts's r2EndpointUrl), so there's nothing else to set here.

# ============================================================
# 3. Local development only — apps/web/.env.local (gitignored; see the audit
#    below for exactly which .env* filenames are and aren't). These are the
#    only values in this file meant to actually be copied into a working
#    local env file as-is.
# ============================================================

# docker-compose.yml maps the container's Postgres to host port 5433 by
# default (not the standard 5432 — deliberately, to avoid colliding with a
# system-wide Postgres install), overridable via OPIKA_DB_PORT. This is a
# throwaway local database — running `pnpm db:seed` against it is exactly
# what it's for, unlike the production string above.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://opika:opika@localhost:5433/opika

# A local value, generated fresh — not copied from Vercel's production
# secret. Cursors signed locally only need to validate locally; there's no
# reason your dev environment should ever hold the real production key.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
CURSOR_HMAC_SECRET=

# Required for `pnpm dev` to serve anything at all, not just a DB-backed
# page — unlike CURSOR_HMAC_SECRET above, apps/web/src/proxy.ts's pre-launch
# gate reads this on every request while SITE_IS_PUBLICLY_DISCOVERABLE is
# false, which is unconditionally true today. A local value, generated
# fresh, same reasoning as CURSOR_HMAC_SECRET: your dev environment never
# needs to hold the real production secret. Generate with: openssl rand -hex
# 32, then open http://localhost:3000/tvaryny?gate=<that value> once to mint
# the cookie for the rest of your session.
PRELAUNCH_GATE_SECRET=

# ============================================================
# Kabinet (shelter cabinet) — optional for adopter-only dev
# ============================================================

# Kabinet sign-in (Better Auth). Without both, /api/auth and /api/kabinet
# answer 503 in dev, never a boot failure. Production signs in only when
# productionSignInOf is on (apps/web/src/kabinet/production-sign-in.ts): a
# production Vercel deployment, every kabinet.* string final, and every
# sign-in variable below set and consistent. A production BUILD fails, and a
# production instance refuses to boot, without EMAIL_PROVIDER, that provider's
# own key, EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS, EMAIL_REPLY_TO, PRODUCTION_ORIGIN,
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET (32+ characters) and BETTER_AUTH_URL (= PRODUCTION_ORIGIN)
# (apps/web/src/kabinet/sign-in-env.ts, IN-R2 Decision 1). Production values:
# docs/h2-next-prs.md's switch-on list. Secret: a local value, generated with
# openssl rand -hex 32. URL: http://localhost:3000 in dev.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
BETTER_AUTH_URL=

# The operator's name as the shelter sees it on operator changes in its
# history, nominative case only (RS-Q2). Unset or blank falls back to
# «Оператор реєстру» from the catalogue.
KABINET_OPERATOR_DISPLAY_NAME=

# Transactional email (invite PR, IN-Q2/IN-Q6). One fetch-based module
# (apps/web/src/kabinet/email-provider.ts), the provider chosen here:
# resend | postmark | brevo. Production is resend for every email (Oleksii,
# 2026-10-15, after delivery test 5: "invites move to Resend; retire Brevo.";
# inbox EM-B10). A provider's key is never set here: each provider reads its
# own variable (RESEND_API_KEY, BREVO_API_KEY, POSTMARK_API_KEY, below), so a
# provider and a key for another provider can't be paired. A provider named
# without its own key is invalid, and production sign-in stays off (fails
# closed). The From address's domain must be exactly mail. +
# PRODUCTION_ORIGIN's host; production sends from noreply@mail.opika.org.ua
# (IN-E1). EMAIL_FROM_NAME is the display name (production: Opika); the name
# is not final, so it stays config. Previews never send (productionSignInOf
# refuses a Preview outright), and no key belongs in Vercel's Preview
# environment either. EMAIL_PROVIDER is the default route: invites, the
# registry's blocked-addresses view, and sign-in unless EMAIL_SIGN_IN_PROVIDER
# says otherwise.
EMAIL_PROVIDER=
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=

# Optional: a different provider for SIGN-IN emails only (EM-B6). Unset (the
# production setting, since both emails are on resend): sign-in uses
# EMAIL_PROVIDER. Set: sign-in goes through that provider, on that provider's
# own key, with the same From address, From name and Reply-To. Setting it to
# EMAIL_PROVIDER's own value changes nothing. That provider's key missing, or
# an unknown value: invalid, and production sign-in stays off (fails closed).
# Kept so one template can be moved back to brevo during Brevo's 30-day grace
# period without a code change.
EMAIL_SIGN_IN_PROVIDER=

# Reply-To on every email (Oleksii, 2026-10-14: "Reply-To: hello@opika.org.ua
# on all emails"). Required wherever a provider is configured, and must be an
# address on PRODUCTION_ORIGIN's own host; production value:
# hello@opika.org.ua. The kabinet sign-in card's "no email? write to me" line
# (kabinet.signInCard.notArrived) names the same address; set it locally to
# see that line in dev, where it is left out when unset.
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=

# Resend's key, under the provider's own name (Oleksii, 2026-10-15, EM-B7):
# the key for every route that names resend. In Vercel: Production only (never
# Preview), a sending-only key restricted to mail.opika.org.ua. The app reads it
# only where a route names resend (EMAIL_PROVIDER or EMAIL_SIGN_IN_PROVIDER);
# on its own it moves nothing. Locally: read from this file (that one key,
# once) by `email:delivery-test`, which sends both emails through Resend by
# default. Never logged, printed or committed.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Brevo's key: the key for any route that names brevo (EM-B7's convention).
# Not needed in Vercel once EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend: Brevo is being retired
# (EM-B10), and its code stays only as the rollback for the 30-day grace
# period. Deleting the key in Brevo and removing it from Vercel (if it was ever
# set there) are retirement steps, each with Oleksii's explicit OK. Locally:
# read by `email:delivery-test` only when --sign-in-provider brevo or
# --invite-provider brevo asks for it. Never logged, printed or committed
# (IN-E1).
BREVO_API_KEY=

# Postmark's key, for a route that names postmark (a candidate in the ADR's
# §12; nothing uses it today). Leave unset.
POSTMARK_API_KEY=
# The production origin, pinned explicitly (IN-R2, Decision 2; never derived
# from VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL). Production value: https://opika.org.ua
# (the apex; www.opika.org.ua redirects 308 to it). Production sign-in needs
# BETTER_AUTH_URL to equal it, and refuses when VERCEL_ENV is missing or
# unknown (fail closed).
PRODUCTION_ORIGIN=

# ============================================================
# Informational — not something you set
# ============================================================

# Set automatically by Next.js / Vercel — never set this yourself. Governs
# the session cookie's __Host- prefix and Secure attribute
# (apps/web/src/api/session/cookie.ts) and this app's own boot-time secrets
# check (apps/web/src/api/env.ts's validateEnv, production only).
# NODE_ENV=production